WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.364 --> 00:00:08.770
[Music]

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:11.895
[Quynh Nguyen, PhD] This particular project,&nbsp;
funded by the National Library of Medicine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.895 --> 00:00:18.522
is producing a new national data resource for&nbsp;
built environment characteristics using &nbsp;

00:00:18.522 --> 00:00:24.600
Google Street View images and computer vision&nbsp;
models and to estimate the association&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:29.098
between built environment characteristics&nbsp;
and health outcomes on a national level.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.800
[Ming Hu] Built environment, in the simplest&nbsp;
way, is just everything human built.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:39.042
It includes the streets, all&nbsp;
the buildings, all the houses.

00:00:39.042 --> 00:00:43.427
[Thu Nguyen] We merged the Google&nbsp;
Street View image data with the patient&nbsp;data.

00:00:43.427 --> 00:00:46.860
So we looked at coronary artery&nbsp;
disease, hypertension, and diabetes.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:51.060
And then our model controlled for individual&nbsp;
characteristics such as like race, ethnicity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:54.546
insurance status, English language ability.

00:00:54.546 --> 00:00:59.485
[Quynh Nguyen] In our pilot study, we merged&nbsp;
those indicators with patient data in Utah.

00:00:59.485 --> 00:01:02.160
It was close to a million patient records.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:06.120
Healthcare systems want to know - what are&nbsp;
some exposures that their patients encounter?&nbsp;

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.640
What are some of the predictors that can help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:11.751
them better understand where's the&nbsp;
chronic risk disease coming from?

00:01:11.751 --> 00:01:16.537
[Thu Nguyen] We found that like greeners&nbsp;
of streets or visible wires or dilapidated&nbsp;&nbsp;buildings

00:01:16.537 --> 00:01:21.645
predicted prevalence of coronary&nbsp;
artery disease and hypertension diabetes.

00:01:21.645 --> 00:01:26.886
[Quynh Nguyen] So crosswalk and sidewalks&nbsp;
are indicators of walkability. So the more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:30.840
walkable neighborhood is, the more&nbsp;
it encourages physical activity.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:35.919
We have other indicators like street trees&nbsp;
and street greenery which promote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.919 --> 00:01:41.000
which we found are associated with, lower&nbsp;
obesity and better mental health.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:45.960
We made a geoportal where you can select the&nbsp;
neighborhood feature that you're interested in.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:51.600
You can also zoom into a location. So you can&nbsp;
type in address or a city and it'll naturally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:55.960
zoom in and give you the distribution of&nbsp;
the characteristics at that neighborhood.

00:01:55.960 --> 00:02:00.300
People can interact with the data.&nbsp;
It allows for a quick analyses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.862
flexible boundaries, and publicly available.

00:02:02.862 --> 00:02:08.450
[Thu Nguyen] And it's a huge data source for for&nbsp;
the public health researchers and policy makers.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:10.858
[Ming Hu] Doing this way, it can give us 

00:02:10.858 --> 00:02:17.685
first, a set of large data to show us what is the impact&nbsp;
of the building we design and we build.

00:02:17.685 --> 00:02:19.720
[Quynh Nguyen] Without NLM support,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:23.279
we wouldn't have the protected&nbsp;
time that we had over five years.

00:02:23.279 --> 00:02:28.500
We wouldn't be able to purchase&nbsp;
the images and also purchase the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.980
the computing software and&nbsp;
hardware to run the models,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:37.752
and also the granted help support - doctoral&nbsp;
students - and fund their their entire studies.

00:02:37.752 --> 00:02:41.399
It takes a significant amount&nbsp;
of time to walk and inventory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.399 --> 00:02:44.459
neighborhood features of the built environment.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:49.378
And so that would not be possible if you&nbsp;
are interested in any place across the U.S.

00:02:49.378 --> 00:02:52.865
And thus, we need computer vision&nbsp;
and Google Street View images to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.865 --> 00:02:55.581
enable the analyses at the national level.

00:02:55.808 --> 00:03:10.551
[Music]

00:03:10.551 --> 00:03:12.930
[Music fades to silence]

00:03:13.052 --> 00:03:15.243
[Silence]

